  ],
  "rationale": "Smoking and pollutant exposure are upstream risk factors. Cancer is a downstream disease outcome that can cause dyspnoea and prompt diagnostic testing. A positive xray result is typically a measurement/diagnostic outcome after disease or symptoms, so it is placed last."
}
